  <section class="hub-section hub-section-gray">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>How our techs approach commercial laundry washers</h2>
      <p>Five failure modes dominate commercial-washer service: drain-pump failure (most common, year 5-8 typical), door-seal (boot) degradation on front-loaders (year 6-10), main control board (often after grid power surges — common in older buildings), drum-bearing wear (year 8-12 — major repair, often pushes economics toward replacement on aging units), and shock-absorber wear (year 4-6 on heavy-use installs). We're EPA 608 certified for any refrigerant-related water-heater integrations and trained on the specific safety lockouts of commercial laundry equipment.</p>
    </div>
