          <summary>My commercial washer won't drain. What's the most common cause?</summary>
          <p>Drain pump failure or a clogged drain hose. We clear the drain-line filter first (catches lint, coins, hair clips), then test the pump. Pump replacement typically $245-$385 with labor. Drain-line clearance is a $145 service call when that's the only issue.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Is Speed Queen really the longest-lasting commercial washer?</summary>
          <p>Yes, in our experience. Speed Queen / UniMac (Alliance Laundry Systems Ripon WI) builds the most durable commercial-grade laundry equipment in the US market. We routinely service 15-20 year-old SC-series units that are still operating reliably. Dexter (Iowa worker cooperative) is the comparable durability tier on the coin-laundry side.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
